@startuml lockfree-cas-architecture
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-cas-architecture.puml — the three moving parts of the lock-free
' overlay: an atomic root cell (the CAS target), the immutable node it points
' at, and a sharded cache for O(1) duplicate detection.
' Source: §Architecture of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' Color key (house palette):
'   slate  #CFD8DC  the atomic root cell (publication slot / CAS target)
'   green  #C8E6C9  the immutable in-memory node
'   teal   #B2DFDB  the lock-free cache (overlay accent)
'   grey   #ECEFF1  the client / infrastructure
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.3
}

title Lock-free ARTrie — atomic root · immutable node · sharded cache

rectangle "**Client thread**\ninsert_cas · contains_lockfree" as C #ECEFF1

package "Lock-free overlay (Arc<T> — no RwLock)" #F5F5F5 {
  rectangle "**AtomicNodePtr** (lockfree_root)\narc-swap root cell · CAS target" as ROOT #CFD8DC
  rectangle "**PersistentNode** (immutable)\nversion · keys · children\nflags (atomic) · value (atomic)" as NODE #C8E6C9
  rectangle "**DashMap** (lockfree_cache)\nTerm → bool · sharded" as CACHE #B2DFDB
}

C -down-> ROOT : load / CAS
C -down-> CACHE : dup check
ROOT -down-> NODE : load() →\nArc snapshot

note bottom of NODE
  A mutation allocates NEW node
  versions (copy-on-write); it never
  mutates a live one. A superseded
  version frees by Arc refcount —
  no EBR required for correctness.
end note
@enduml
